  "identity": "Exactly THREE ivory skulls mounted on ONE shared tall crooked spine, broad ribcage and one floating ragged dark maroon choir robe. Center skull proud, left skull flat off-key, right skull perpetually a beat late. Tiny bony conductor hands. No legs, no extra skulls, no separate creatures. Warm bone and cool grey recesses, gold chipped choir brooch.",
  "definition_header": "name THE BONE CHOIR\ntext Three skulls on one spine, singing in a key that hurts. They have been rehearsing since before the Crypt was dug.\nby angelX\nwhere crypt\nhp 700\nsize 1.4\nmove hover speed=1.4\nattack ring shots=12 speed=4 every=140 damage=10 shot=bone\nattack aimed shots=3 speed=6 every=70 damage=11 shot=orb\nphases gap_ring burst flower every=72 volleys=2 damage=10 shot=bone\nrage 35%\ndrops bone 6, wax 3, gold 190",
